[gd_resource type="Resource" script_class="ManualPage" load_steps=2 format=3]

[ext_resource type="Script" path="res://src/components/manual_page.gd" id="1_page"]

[resource]
script = ExtResource("1_page")
title = "DAMAGE CONTROL"
body = "THE HULL is xenon-metal. Service accessible fittings and patch breaches; do not cut into the sealed primary structure.

MICRO-PUNCTURES raise the compartment leak rate; pressure falls, and leaks keep working while you sleep. Each occupied compartment has a wall-mounted patch point. Use the point in the leaking compartment; a patch elsewhere does not seal that room. MAIN on the readout means the life-support compartment.

PATCH PROCEDURE
  At the leaking room's patch point, press {interact} for each prompt:
  1  CLEAN THE BREACH
  2  FIT THE PATCH
  3  APPLY SEALANT (one charge from the carried cartridge)
  4  VERIFY SEAL
Check STATUS for fewer punctures and reduced leak rate. A patch seals one puncture, not all leaks; repeat if more remain. Some background leakage remains even in a sound compartment.

Take a charged sealant cartridge before you go; it must be in your hands at the seal step. An empty shell cannot seal. Fabricate a sealant charge, then refill the carried shell at the fabricator. The hull will not wait for a second trip."
